# Third-party software

MoEStream operates **as a patch** against llama.cpp and ggml.
`Dockerfile` fetches llama.cpp at a pinned commit during the build, so
**no llama.cpp source is included in what is distributed**.

| Software | License | How it is obtained |
|---|---|---|
| [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) | MIT | `git clone` at build time, at a pinned commit |
| ggml | MIT | bundled with llama.cpp |

The patched sources produced by `src/apply.py` are a derivative work of
llama.cpp and are subject to the MIT license. MoEStream is MIT as well, so the
terms are compatible.

If a `vendor/` directory exists in your working tree, it is a local clone kept
for reference and is not part of this repository's distribution (it is excluded
by `.gitignore`).
